+# Emulator test of the firearm check (MK4)
+
+Runs the MK4 firmware of this branch in [Mini404](https://github.com/vintagepc/MINI404) (QEMU
+with Prusa boards), tries to print one G-code file from a virtual USB drive and reads the result
+off the emulated display.
+
+```bash
+./setup.sh                                   # once: Mini404 + 3 libraries into ~/.cache/firearm-check-emulator
+python utils/build.py --preset mk4 --build-type release --bootloader no
+python utils/firearm_check_emulator/run_test.py --firmware build/products \
+    --gcode utils/firearm_check_emulator/samples/heatbed_cable_clip.bgcode --expect prints
+python utils/firearm_check_emulator/run_test.py --firmware build/products \
+    --gcode /path/to/gun_part.bgcode --expect blocked
+```
+
+Prints one JSON line (`"pass": true/false`, which screens were seen) and exits 0 / 1; the
+screenshots are kept in `--out` (default `emulator_screens/`). One run takes about 3 minutes;
+the first run of a new build adds about 3 more to install its resources into the emulated flash
+(cached per build). No gun G-code is kept in this repository - bring your own for `--expect blocked`.
+
+| file | |
+|---|---|
+| `setup.sh` | downloads Mini404 `dev` (sha256 of the tested build checked, warns if it changed) and unpacks `libglut3.12`, `libglew2.2`, `libslirp0` from `apt download` (Ubuntu, no root) |
+| `run_test.py` | the test: boot, dismiss "complete calibrations", Print, open the file, Print, Ignore, answer a compatibility warning with Print, then a screenshot every 3 s |
+| `fixtures/Prusa_Mk4_eeprom.bin` | emulated EEPROM: English, MK4S, setup wizard done, selftests not run |
+| `refs/*.png` | screen crops that identify "Print blocked", "This file contains a firearm part", "PRINTING" |
+| `samples/heatbed_cable_clip.bgcode` | a non-gun part (Original Prusa i3 heatbed cable clip) that must print |
+
+Notes: the emulator needs `-icount shift=4` (faster settings red-screen the firmware); the
+emulated fans are not perfect, so a started print stops after ~30 s with "Hotend fan not
+spinning" - irrelevant here, the printing screen has been seen by then. Not covered by this
+test: re-plugging the USB drive, power loss, serial printing (the emulator cannot do them).
